@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280

title Facility Detail page (page-type flow)\nOpening one organization on the same terms as a provider: brought to live freshness, still shown when the registry is silent, reconciled against its one required member.

actor "Person / Client" as User
participant "Gate\n(facade, transport only)" as Gate
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices main)" as UN
database "Repository\nsession, render ledger, page state" as Repo
participant "facility_detail\n(tool, required member)" as FD
participant "Authoritative registry\n(live query by NPI)" as NPPES
database "Facility record\ncollection" as DB
participant "Prose tool\n(member, authors the sentence)" as Prose

User -> Gate : click a facility card's link\n{ session_token, head, params(openNpi) }
activate Gate
note over Gate
  A click, not an utterance. The gate collects the session token,
  the HTTP head, and the parameters, each if present, and hands
  them on. It owns no route and verifies nothing.
end note
Gate -> UN : navigate(session_token, head, params)
activate UN

note right of UN
  TRIAGE by declared proof. Five ways a call may arrive:
  tool_to_tool (none), client_sessioned (session_token),
  third_party_callback (api_key), static_witness (none),
  internal_callback (our_signature). A session token is
  present -> this is a client_sessioned arrival.
end note
UN -> Repo : verify session_token, advance the nonce
Repo --> UN : session ok

note right of UN
  DETERMINE THE PAGE from the live registry map: openNpi names
  a record whose entity is an organization -> the facility page.
  The UN holds no data; the map is the registry, page state a
  repository row.
end note
UN -> Repo : page state = facility page shows this NPI

note right of UN
  OPEN THE RENDER LEDGER. Record the page's required_members
  as the expectation and race the completeness budget against
  the completion callback:
    members          = { facility_detail, prose }
    required_members = { facility_detail }
    budget           = completeness.render_timeout_seconds
end note
UN -> Repo : record ledger expectation { facility_detail }, start the budget

alt facility_detail returns within the budget
  UN -> FD : dispatch(openNpi)
  activate FD

  FD -> NPPES : query by NPI (live freshness on open)
  activate NPPES
  NPPES --> FD : live record, or nothing
  deactivate NPPES

  alt the authoritative registry answered
    alt the NPI is an organization
      FD -> DB : read the stored record
      DB --> FD : record as we hold it
      FD -> FD : project both onto the registry-owned fields and compare;\nmerge from OUR record, applying only the registry's fields\n(never a person attribute onto a facility; never a tax identifier)
      opt the merge changed something real
        FD -> DB : replace the record, read it back
        DB --> FD : the record as now stored
      end
    else the NPI is not an organization
      FD -> Prose : author "facility not found"
      Prose --> FD : the not-found sentence
      note right of FD
        No Facility Detail is shown for an NPI the authoritative
        registry reports is not an organization; the user is told
        the facility was not found.
      end note
    end
  else the authoritative registry did not answer
    FD -> DB : read the stored record
    DB --> FD : record as we hold it (shown with no comparison)
    note right of FD
      A detail is still shown when the source does not answer.
      Not answering leaves us no reason to doubt the record.
    end note
  end

  FD -> FD : build the panel\n- legal business name; other name and its label; NPI; NPI issue date; active\n- parent's legal business name when the facility is a subpart\n- classification label, specialization, plain-language definition\n- authorized official (last, first, middle, title, credential), so labelled\n- destinations to confirm the enumeration and the right to operate
  FD --> UN : internal_callback { panel }  proof our_signature
  deactivate FD

  UN -> Repo : close the ledger entry for facility_detail
  UN -> UN : RECONCILE - every required member closed;\nserial deterministic merge of returning documents\n(a parameter/state conflict RAISES -> on_conflict)
  opt prose member
    UN -> Prose : author the panel's summary, with the facts
    activate Prose
    Prose --> UN : the user-facing sentence
    deactivate Prose
  end
  UN --> Gate : the reconciled facility panel

else the budget expires first  (on_timeout)
  UN -> Prose : author the layman on_timeout explanation
  activate Prose
  Prose --> UN : "we could not bring this facility up in time - please try again"
  deactivate Prose
  UN --> Gate : respond anyway, the page unrendered
  note right of UN
    The completeness timeout races the callback. On expiry the
    UN responds in layman's terms, instrumented with timings at
    a severity matching impact.
  end note

else facility_detail dies or never calls back  (on_missing_required)
  UN -> UN : render ledger RAISES - the one required member is missing;\ncatch, classify, log with timings
  UN --> Gate : ChatHealthyException surfaced
  note right of UN
    Every throw ends in a UniversalNavigator. A required member
    that dies or never returns leaves the page unreconcilable.
  end note
end

[<-- Gate : the one stream the gate writes
deactivate UN
Gate --> User : the facility as the registry reports it now
deactivate Gate

@enduml
